{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117601","id":3417289105,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7Lr7GR","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117601","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117601.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117601.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117601","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117601/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117601/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117601/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6830f48662e1096ce40be171dbd1b543eca020ff","number":117601,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add `BitField[T]` type to GDScript","user":{"login":"GabCoolDude","id":123309403,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1mNWw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123309403?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude","html_url":"https://github.com/GabCoolDude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GabCoolDude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR introduces an analyzer-only type called `BitField`, used to determine if an enum should be treated as a bitfield, to GDScript.\r\n\r\n- Gives `PROPERTY_HINT_FLAGS` and `PROPERTY_USAGE_CLASS_IS_BITFIELD` to variables of this type.\r\n- Ignores `ENUM_VARIABLE_WITHOUT_DEFAULT`, `INT_AS_ENUM_WITHOUT_CAST` and `INT_AS_ENUM_WITHOUT_MATCH`.\r\n- **Must** have one collection type (which has to be an enum), unlike other collection types that are currently supported.\r\n- At runtime and compile-time, it is treated as a regular integer.\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n```gdscript\r\nenum MyEnum {\r\n    FIRST = 1 << 0,\r\n    SECOND = 1 << 1,\r\n    THIRD = 1 << 2,\r\n    FOURTH = 1 << 3    \r\n}\r\n\r\n@export var bitfield: BitField[MyEnum]\r\n# This has the same effect, but has weaker static typing and can be annoying to setup for larger enums\r\n@export_flags(\"First\", \"Second\", \"Third\", \"Fourth\") var flags: int\r\n\r\n# Obviously, it's not restricted to just being used in @export, \r\n# although I don't see much of a point, other than for documentation purposes.\r\nfunc my_func(param: BitField[MyEnum]) -> BitField[MyEnum]:\r\n    return MyEnum.FIRST | MyEnum.SECOND\r\n\r\nsignal my_signal(param: BitField[MyEnum])\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is also _technically_ the first collection type to support being nested, but since it's just treated as an int at compile-time, it doesn't really count in my book:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar array: Array[BitField[EnumName]]\r\nvar dict: Dictionary[BitField[EnumName], BitField[EnumName]]\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, due to this not being a real type, it cannot have methods to make usage easier. What would be an ideal implementation is making [the existing BitField type in the core](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/templates/bit_field.h) available in GDScript, but this would require a much more complicated implementation, which is probably not worth it.\r\n\r\nKnown issues:\r\n- Trying to ctrl+click on a `BitField` type in the script editor does not lead to it's documentation page, unlike other types. I can't seem to figure out where the logic for this is.\r\n\r\nSupersedes #117381.\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/923.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"